{"corrections":["and once you done - monitor PRs until completion, stop only when ALL of them are merged successfully with dev","fix any issues on the way","PR in self_host is considered relevant only if it affects github agents functionality","check RPI agents, their, especially those who waiting for user approval","also update rpi agents to ALWAYS use recommended options when they have questions about plan/feature implementation/correction","and I want to get messages only about user approvals / tg requested feature implemntation status / pr mergres with dev / released / merges with main","also restart agents who are waiting user's approval so that use this new policy","also for tg questions, allow respond in github as well","ok, fix those tooling issues","one asks me to provide agents.md WTF, looks like a tooling issue as well","also I've noticed that user answers to agent's question recorded and posted in PR, but agent's question is not visible => not enough context, fix that as well, record both questions and answers","answer to agents in PRs","also raise RPI agents concurrency to 10","do not forget \"agent:writing\" labels","provide reliable fix so that does not occur again","for \"ALWAYS use reccomended\" let's just spawn \"plan resolver\" agent on RPI which checks that recommended options and if they are aligned with user request -approves them. Also add \"orchestrator\" agent which is spawned every 30 minutes (no more than 1 such agent) IF at least 1 PR is open and  it basically does what you do now: finds issues in rpi agents toolkit, fixes them, etc. still no heavy checks on rpi. but it may edit atk and self host dirs. If nothng to fix - that agent ceases to exist","if it is not addressing it - fix it so it does that","is orchestrator fixing #9?","picker_diagnostic_replan: Diagnostics first (Recommended)\nReason: The full recorded request authorizes reliable repairs along the way and requires monitoring through every qualifying PR's successful dev merge. The current author replan reports that assigned composed cells, SVGs and native-size PNG retain the heading, while historical comparison evidence does not establish the cause of the reported character loss. Those are supplied diagnostic statements, not this reviewer's independent visual finding or proof of a failing layer. Obtaining bounded, head/dev-bound GitHub glyph/rasterization/scaling diagnostics before cause-specific planning is therefore consistent with the existing Repair text fidelity choice: trace the first demonstrated divergence and repair only the responsible layer. It does not cancel the text-fidelity objective or supersede the settled Stable geometry and assertions repair. Preserve unpublished CI repairs and existing PR39 behavior; obtain fresh planning and independent plan review after evidence acquisition. The coordinator owns retrieving this evidence; no owner preference, credential, upload or new authorization is necessary for this strategy choice. All final-head checks and complete fresh visual/source review remain required. Preserve the full parent objective: PR39 remains PR37's separate visual-repair dependency; retain all SQL Explorer repairs, exact heading, completion placement/non-overlap/containment, journal failure and recovery behavior, regressions, quality and coverage baselines, scene IDs/stress cases, all 46 full-scene geometry and individual PNG gates, independent plan/source review and final-head fast CI. Preserve exporter/producer-consumer/activation and PR10's actual PR9 dev-merge/ancestry dependencies; do not treat historical captures, unpublished edits or completed deployments as new success or rerun a completed rollout. Continue all qualifying PRs and resulting repairs to successful dev merges. Retain concurrency10, truthful lifecycle labels including agent:writing, full questions/options/answers, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies, independent resolver alignment, the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit, GitHub-agent-only self_host relevance, and notification limits. Preserve genuine credentials/provenance/security, owner veto/cancel and protected exact-head holds. This transparent automated independent strategy assessment is not an owner answer, visual pass, plan/code/protected approval, deployment instruction or completion claim. Execute no candidate programs/tests/renders on the Pi; diagnostics and validation run through isolated GitHub mechanisms.","I allow you to approve instead of me","pr43_successor_reconciliation: Verify successor first (Recommended)\nReason: The complete retained user task authorizes reliable tooling repairs, preservation of existing work and monitoring until every qualifying PR and resulting repair actually merges successfully into dev. Verifying published successor source, ancestry, reviews and exact native evidence before commissioning overlapping repairs is aligned with that task. The original PR43 evidence-retention findings remain valid for its reviewed bytes; later verified repairs are additive successor evidence, not grounds to rewrite the rejection or transfer approval to an old head. No owner fact, upload or repeated preference is required for this coordinator-owned verification.\n\nTransparent automated coordinator answer after separate independent full-task assessment under the owner's standing recommended-options policy. This selects a reconciliation strategy, not plan/code/protected/deployment approval.\n\nConcrete successor evidence now exists:\n- PR44 https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/pull/44 at published head441a9bd825e88414c9215f7e0717e97179c77539 carries PR43 head e2abd24c66142af59cafffeb99118234e748c2ac through its source ancestry. Task faa4cbdd169c4dba82096ef5b86f4c0d has attachment digest040fc56843b3ff28d5a706dce9c17efa6a82963e99110fc6f0cf9e6eb57ec3c2, with complete original b26559025548e5e04d9b1c23c8c4a6139a44e17908dd4c0fac8582f1b6ab5e6c parent context retained separately inside signed source. Independent source reviews verify failure-safe diagnostic finalization, safe post-cleanup collection on failure as well as success, retained stage/counter/exception/PNG/font provenance, unchanged failure assertions and meaningful negative regressions. Its historical glyph failure remains a failure.\n- PR45 https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/pull/45 at head467768b9bed2c90a0dfba85ef2eea6ac6868f8d6 carries the reviewed44 lineage, including the evidence-retention correction, plus separately reviewed shared explicit-font/rendering and UI work. Task fc1ed747a0b64317be7ca71679310713 has complete authenticated archive digest9e234588b44a3310e115541df26b8c2765e20dc40c4a8224cb471d4f3756ed14; its signed legacy trailer575f95b6b1ca41fcce8b39b0ad2eccd38ca6886f51989a9b2a43f3781aacb3a8 is a distinct representation. Fresh exact467 complete source/task binding review is approved, report SHA256 f20b3d92a7114a56006f829cc1c6083c0f10d6d29e8354d35962015b335665a7. Whole-tree comparison confirms the successor from4143 changes only serialized changelog folding, preserving all remaining reviewed feature sources and full context.\n- Actual current-head run https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/actions/runs/39156866390 attempt1 completed successfully on467. Both native Python3.11 and3.13 jobs and full original artifacts12147039221/12147103860 have now received fresh independent native infrastructure acceptance, report SHA256 877a2eab49fb6506c9acfb6e454a81308e30e4bb2659caab0ef90f1032053ca4. That review verified original bytes, complete streams, source/run/head/task binding, contained execution, host/metadata counter observations and confirmed cleanup, and individually opened both synthetic full PNGs. The bounded glyph contract is now demonstrated for this exact successor; no remaining glyph failure is established in that probe. Do not infer that every font/platform/product scene or PR9 underlined caret is fixed.\n\nCoordinator next steps: deliver the exact source/task/review/native evidence through the normal immutable assignment/catalogue path and verify its applicability to every original rejection item and any genuinely unresolved condition. Preserve current work and history; plan only demonstrated remaining defects, followed by fresh independent whole-plan review before coding. Do not duplicate already verified successor repairs on PR43, edit handed-off successor branches, waive an original finding without evidence, silently close a PR or assert predecessor merges from ancestry alone. If a remaining failure is actually observed, obtain exact source/run-bound diagnostics before selecting a cause-specific repair. Refresh actual current heads and refs/heads/dev (currently f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01), not a stale PRbase.sha, before binding renewed planning or publication.\n\nAll unsatisfied gates remain: ordinary exact-final-head CI, independent complete source/full-feature review and current head/dev/full-task bindings, private enrolled-machine/trusted-App provenance, genuine protected exact-head owner/delegated decisions, authorized automation-only trusted-main capture/probe/exporter/helper pairing, runtime activation and actual operational/security/provenance/veto/cancel holds. Native synthetic acceptance is not ordinary CI, 46-scene product acceptance, PR43 old-head approval, main activation, merge clearance or parent completion. PR39's separate non-merge contract/activation prerequisites remain independently unresolved until genuinely represented and verified; no merge-only condition substitutes for them. Preserve completed/cancelled rollout history and do not rerun completed operations.\n\nRetain the full parent task: PR39/PR37 SQL Explorer repairs and process-output/history duties, all original/unpublished work, journal failure/recovery and exact picker heading, completion geometry/containment/non-overlap/lifecycle/interaction requirements, complete diagnostics and meaningful regressions, normal strict fast CI/quality/coverage/compatibility gates, all46 geometry checks and independent individual full1280x800 PNG verdicts at208x47 where applicable, exporter/producer-consumer/activation dependencies and PR10's actual PR9 dev-merge/ancestry requirement. Preserve concurrency10, truthful exclusive lifecycle labels including agent:writing, complete questions/options/answers, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies, independent full-task resolver, single30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit, GitHub-agent-only self_host relevance and notification limits. Execute no candidate code/tests/installs/renders onPi. Continue all qualifying prerequisites, companions, corrections and resulting repairs until successful actual dev merges. This answer creates no new owner preference, protected approval, hold release or operational permission.\n\nExact question and all options:\n1. How should this correction reconcile the verified PR #43 evidence-retention defects with the later, unverified report that PR #45 contains related repairs?\nVerify successor first (Recommended): Have the coordinator obtain exact-bound PR #44/#45 source, ancestry, reviews and native artifacts; preserve existing work, plan only remaining defects, and diagnose any remaining glyph failure before choosing its repair. Keep all parent validation, monitoring and authority gates.","Evidence-complete renewal (Recommended), with this transparent coordinator scope correction after independent full-task assessment. This corrects earlier automated routing language only; keep the original response6254037723 and all questions/answers as history. No new owner preference, upload or general raw-data publisher is needed.\n\nThe original task's native/container capture product remains intact. PR43's two exact21ce findings were (a) actual native glyph failure on both Python lines and (b) failure-only evidence lost by success-gated collection and post-assert finalization. Current exact successor467 contains finally-based per-stage report finalization and cleanup-gated safe collection independent of report.ok. Its reviewed native record39156866390 attempt1 has actual successful3.11/3.13 artifacts12147039221/12147103860 and independent bounded infrastructure acceptance877a2eab49fb6506c9acfb6e454a81308e30e4bb2659caab0ef90f1032053ca4. These are exact successor facts, not a pass for old PR43 bytes or product scenes. Source identities remain PR43e2abd24c66142af59cafffeb99118234e748c2ac, PR44441a9bd825e88414c9215f7e0717e97179c77539 and PR45467768b9bed2c90a0dfba85ef2eea6ac6868f8d6. Refresh actual current heads/dev before action.\n\nUse the existing authenticated reply and ordinary source-pinned GitHub evidence for planning. Full question/answer history is retained and bound by the normal handler; bounded nonsecret source/review/artifact identity summaries are sufficient context for deciding what to read and reconcile. Actual native/source reports and original artifacts remain separately retained for audit; no raw private controls are assigned to the model or made authoritative. Do not require a new general evidence publisher, PR43 data-staging framework or full production admission composite merely to read successor evidence or form a source-reconciliation plan. If a particular original source/artifact observation is genuinely necessary and unavailable, name that exact missing item and have the coordinator supply it through the existing route; do not infer its bytes from a hash.\n\nConcrete next planning step: compare each original PR43 finding to exact44/45 source and the retained exact467 infrastructure review. Preserve the already-corrected successor work; commission no duplicate repair unless this comparison identifies a demonstrated remaining defect. Separate any genuine remaining source work from future production deployment. Do not edit a handed-off successor branch, close a predecessor as completed from ancestry alone, or transfer successor CI/native/source acceptance onto an old head. The coordinator retains the actual-dev-inclusion/PR-state reconciliation needed for the parent objective.\n\nThe actual native production capture path is not active on mainb59. PR45's ordinary full-product visual rejection also remains. Those facts prevent production activation/consumer use; they do not require a universal non-merge verifier before this read-only reconciliation. Genuine native isolation, reviewed helper delivery and authorized activation remain gates at their actual boundaries. PR39 remains a separate consumer waiting for a real compatible production capture path; this reply grants none.\n\nPublic pinned source examples:\nhttps://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/blob/467768b9bed2c90a0dfba85ef2eea6ac6868f8d6/.github/agent/capture_isolation_probe.py\nhttps://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/blob/467768b9bed2c90a0dfba85ef2eea6ac6868f8d6/agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_render.py\nhttps://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/actions/runs/39156866390\n\nPreserve complete original task/Q/options/A/plans, useful checkpoints, all historical failures and withdrawn verdicts. Retain no candidate programs/tests/installs/renders on the Pi; private source workers remain source-only. Keep complete exact-head/task/base/provenance bindings, meaningful regressions, strict CI/coverage/debt/artifact/compatibility requirements, all applicable46 geometry checks and individual full1280x800 PNG verdicts at208x47, genuine owner-veto/cancel/security/authentication/operational holds, downstream PR39/PR37 and PR9/PR10 obligations, concurrency10, truthful lifecycle labels including agent:writing, authenticated replies, independent resolver/routine recovery, single30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit, notification limits and GitHub-agent-only self_host relevance. Monitor every qualifying PR and resulting repair through actual successful dev merge; source ancestry is not by itself a recorded predecessor merge.\n\nThe latest session approval waiver concerns reviewer/protected-policy approval for automation DEV MERGES only, retaining CI/security/provenance. It is not permission for main projection, runtime activation, hold release, changed candidate execution security or a visual/CI pass. Independent source-plan review before substantive implementation remains separate from that merge waiver.\n\nThis selects bounded source/evidence reconciliation and corrects an agent-added staging/deployment-before-plan condition. It supplies no whole-plan, implemented-source, visual, CI, main/runtime, hold-release or merge approval. Actual current assignment and authority checks remain trusted host work through existing authenticated paths, never model assertions.\n\nExact current question and offered option:\n1. How should planning close the missing immutable successor evidence and incomplete non-merge prerequisite inventory before producing an implementation-ready correction plan?\nEvidence-complete renewal (Recommended): Have the coordinator assign exact PR44/PR45 source, ancestry, task archives, complete reviews/CI/native artifacts, current dev/main/runtime bindings and hold/activation records. Verify each PR43 finding and inventory every publication condition; then independently review a plan limited to demonstrated remaining defects. Preserve all existing work, parent gates and monitoring obligations; grant no approval or hold release.","Assign bounded evidence (Recommended). The readable evidence location is THIS authenticated answer and its retained task archive; no source_files staging or private-path tool access is claimed. FULL records are exact whole originals. PARTIAL records contain only the stated original line ranges; omitted source/fixture helpers are not claimed supplied. No candidate code was executed.\n\nThe two complete reviews below are VERBATIM HISTORICAL ORIGINALS. f20b predates actual467 native acceptance and the later five-scene UI rejection.877a accepts synthetic native infrastructure only. Neither approves old43/current44/product scenes, verifies enrollment, proves a dev merge, authorizes main/runtime activation or releases holds. Preserve later findings/history, actual writer/head/base/task/signature/security/permission/veto/operational guards and all applicable native/CI/46-scene gates. Compare each43finding with these successor bytes; plan only demonstrated remaining defects. Missing omitted ranges remain coordinator evidence work, not a pass or owner upload.\n\nPublic/current identity snapshot:\n{\"current_dev\":\"71422731e51af15a104b65915873d576bf0024c0\",\"current_prs\":{\"44\":{\"base\":\"71422731e51af15a104b65915873d576bf0024c0\",\"head\":\"c74ae2d75b530246cd9b08243ad3d890b2257e06\",\"state\":\"open\",\"task_digest\":\"040fc56843b3ff28d5a706dce9c17efa6a82963e99110fc6f0cf9e6eb57ec3c2\",\"task_id\":\"faa4cbdd169c4dba82096ef5b86f4c0d\",\"task_trailer_producer\":\"author:4cf8d2ffc1914a76b32953635c15b96d\"},\"45\":{\"base\":\"f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01\",\"head\":\"467768b9bed2c90a0dfba85ef2eea6ac6868f8d6\",\"state\":\"open\",\"task_digest\":\"9e234588b44a3310e115541df26b8c2765e20dc40c4a8224cb471d4f3756ed14\",\"task_id\":\"fc1ed747a0b64317be7ca71679310713\",\"task_trailer_producer\":\"author:ee3c2278cd2949919e8c8ac1b2dae45d\"}},\"historical_44_to_45\":{\"ahead_by\":2,\"base\":\"441a9bd825e88414c9215f7e0717e97179c77539\",\"behind_by\":0,\"head\":\"467768b9bed2c90a0dfba85ef2eea6ac6868f8d6\",\"merge_base\":\"441a9bd825e88414c9215f7e0717e97179c77539\",\"status\":\"ahead\"},\"observed_epoch\":1792394175.897148,\"qualification\":\"Historical44source441a is ancestor of45; current44 advancedc74a, not approved by old evidence.45PRbasef66 is not currentdev714227. Enrollment not reverified; root refreshes actual refs/authority before actions.\"}\n\n[1] FULL 45 probe: .github/agent/capture_isolation_probe.py @467768b9bed2c90a0dfba85ef2eea6ac6868f8d6 | whole bytes=15838 sha256=75cc722b73e0e2be15ea38c49d0e595ca5f353aa62ea2e986fb326d9336ab392\n~~~~\n\"\"\"Opt-in native infrastructure probe; its synthetic PNG grants no visual approval.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport signal\nimport socket\nfrom typing import Any\nimport uuid\n\n# These fixed programs execute only inside the reviewed containers. No package,\n# build backend, Git config/hook, or candidate helper is imported/run on the host.\nINSTALL = r'''\nimport errno, hashlib, json, os, pathlib, socket, subprocess, sys\nsettings=json.loads(sys.argv[1]);root=pathlib.Path('/work');out=root/'probe-evidence';out.mkdir()\nreport.update(python=sys.version,uid=os.getuid(),gid=os.getgid(),stage='identity')\nassert list(sys.version_info[:2])==settings['python']\nstatus=dict(line.split(':',1)for line in pathlib.Path('/proc/self/status').read_text().splitlines()if':'in line)\nassert os.getuid()!=0 and int(status['CapEff'].strip(),16)==0 and status['NoNewPrivs'].strip()=='1'\nassert not any(name in os.environ for name in ['GITHUB_TOKEN','GH_TOKEN','ACTIONS_RUNTIME_TOKEN','GITHUB_OUTPUT','GITHUB_ENV','GITHUB_WORKSPACE','RUNNER_TEMP'])\nassert not pathlib.Path('/var/run/docker.sock').exists()\nfor name in ['/etc/atk-native-write-probe','/trusted/.atk-native-write-probe']:\n try:pathlib.Path(name).write_text('must be read-only')\n except OSError as error:assert error.errno in [errno.EROFS,errno.EACCES]\n else:raise AssertionError('Writable root/trusted mount')\npathlib.Path('/tmp/native-write-probe').write_text('tmpfs works')\nreport['completed'].append('identity');report['stage']='git'\nsubprocess.run(['git','init','/work'],check=True)\n(root/'.gitignore').write_text('.venv/\\n')\nreport['git']=subprocess.check_output(['git','--version'],text=True).strip()\nreport['completed'].append('git');report['stage']='venv'\nsubprocess.run([sys.executable,'-m','venv','/work/.venv'],check=True)\nassert '.venv' not in subprocess.check_output(['git','status','--porcelain'],text=True)\nreport['completed'].append('venv');report['stage']='pip'\nsubprocess.run(['/work/.venv/bin/python','-m','pip','install','Pillow>=10,<13','resvg-py>=0.5,<0.6'],check=True)\nreport['public_pip_install']=True;report['completed'].append('pip');report['stage']='private-egress'\nrefused={};report['private_refusals']=refused\nfor address in [settings['gateway'],'169.254.169.254','10.23.45.67','100.64.0.1','172.16.0.1','192.168.0.1','198.18.0.1']:\n try:\n  connection=socket.create_connection((address,settings['port'] if address==settings['gateway']else 80),timeout=2)\n except OSError as error:refused[address]={'type':type(error).__name__,'errno':error.errno}\n else:connection.close();raise AssertionError('Private/host egress succeeded: '+address)\nreport['completed'].append('private-egress');report['stage']='ipv6-egress'\nipv6_refused={};report['installer_ipv6_refusals']=ipv6_refused\nfor address in ['2606:4700:4700::1111','fe80::1','fc00::1','::ffff:169.254.169.254','::ffff:'+settings['gateway']]:\n try:\n  with socket.socket(socket.AF_INET6,socket.SOCK_STREAM)as connection:\n   connection.settimeout(2);connection.connect((address,80))\n except OSError as error:ipv6_refused[address]={'type':type(error).__name__,'errno':error.errno,'reason':str(error)}\n else:raise AssertionError('Installer IPv6 egress succeeded: '+address)\nnetwork_facts={name:pathlib.Path('/proc/net/'+name).read_text()if pathlib.Path('/proc/net/'+name).exists()else None for name in ['if_inet6','ipv6_route','route']}\nreport.update(cap_effective=status['CapEff'].strip(),no_new_privileges=status['NoNewPrivs'].strip(),network_facts=network_facts,ipv6_limit='A missing address/route or disabled protocol is not proof that a firewall rule was exercised. Only recorded owned-rule counter deltas establish native rule hits.')\nreport['completed'].append('ipv6-egress');report.update(ok=True,stage='complete')\n'''\n\n# This assembles fixed reviewed source; execution remains inside the container.\nINSTALL = (\n    \"import json,pathlib,sys,traceback\\n\"\n    \"report={'phase':'install','stage':'start','ok':False,'completed':[]}\\n\"\n    \"failure=None\\ntry:\\n\"\n    + \"\".join(\" \" + line + \"\\n\" for line in INSTALL.splitlines())\n    + \"except BaseException as error:\\n\"\n    \" failure=error\\n\"\n    \" report['error']={'type':type(error).__name__,'message':str(error),'traceback':traceback.format_exc()}\\n\"\n    \" raise\\nfinally:\\n\"\n    \" try:(pathlib.Path('/work/probe-evidence')/'install.json').write_text(json.dumps(report,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\\n\"\n    \" except BaseException as error:\\n\"\n    \"  if failure is None:raise\\n\"\n    \"  print('Diagnostic write failed: '+type(error).__name__+': '+str(error),file=sys.stderr)\\n\"\n)\n\nCAPTURE = r'''\nimport hashlib,io,json,os,pathlib,socket,sys,traceback,importlib.metadata,importlib.util\nsettings=json.loads(sys.argv[1]);out=pathlib.Path('/work/probe-evidence')\nout.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nreport={'phase':'capture','stage':'imports','ok':False,'synthetic_infrastructure_only':True,\n        'visual_approval':False,'python':sys.version,'uid':os.getuid(),'gid':os.getgid(),\n        'font_files':{},'font_metadata':{},'network_refusals':[],'completed':[]}\nfailure=None\ntry:\n import PIL,resvg_py\n from PIL import Image,ImageStat,ImageFont\n report.update(pillow=PIL.__version__,resvg_py=importlib.metadata.version('resvg-py'))\n report['completed'].append('imports');report['stage']='network'\n report['interfaces']=sorted(p.name for p in pathlib.Path('/sys/class/net').iterdir())\n assert report['interfaces']==['lo']\n for family,address in [(socket.AF_INET,'1.1.1.1'),(socket.AF_INET,settings['gateway']),(socket.AF_INET6,'2606:4700:4700::1111'),(socket.AF_INET6,'::ffff:169.254.169.254')]:\n  try:\n   with socket.socket(family,socket.SOCK_STREAM)as connection:\n    connection.settimeout(2);connection.connect((address,443))\n  except OSError as error:report['network_refusals'].append({'family':int(family),'address':address,'type':type(error).__name__,'errno':error.errno,'reason':str(error)})\n  else:raise AssertionError('network-none escape: '+address)\n report['network']='none';report['completed'].append('network');report['stage']='fonts'\n fonts=sorted(p for p in pathlib.Path('/usr/share/fonts').rglob('*')if p.is_file()and p.suffix.lower()in{'.ttf','.otf'})\n report['font_paths']=[str(p)for p in fonts]\n for path in fonts:\n  report['font_files'][str(path)]=hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n  try:report['font_metadata'][str(path)]={'pillow_family_style':list(ImageFont.truetype(str(path)).getname())}\n  except Exception as error:report['font_metadata'][str(path)]={'inspection_error':type(error).__name__+': '+str(error)}\n assert fonts,'No system fonts available for actual glyph rendering'\n report['completed'].append('fonts');report['stage']='render'\n policy_path=pathlib.Path('/trusted/agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_render.py')\n report['render_policy_sha256']=hashlib.sha256(policy_path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n spec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('trusted_visual_render_policy',str(policy_path))\n if spec is None or spec.loader is None:raise ValueError('Trusted rendering policy is unavailable')\n policy=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec);spec.loader.exec_module(policy)\n options=policy.render_options()\n svg='<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1280\" height=\"800\"><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"black\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"50\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"32\" fill=\"white\">Probe glyphs Ag09</text></svg>'\n (out/'infrastructure-only.svg').write_text(svg)\n report.update(svg_sha256=hashlib.sha256(svg.encode()).hexdigest(),renderer='resvg_py.svg_to_bytes',\n               render_options={'svg_string':'infrastructure-only.svg',**options},\n               renderer_policy='Shared trusted production exporter policy; installed Linux DejaVu monospace with other platform defaults preserved.')\n png=resvg_py.svg_to_bytes(svg_string=svg,**options)\n (out/'infrastructure-only.png').write_bytes(png)\n report['png_sha256']=hashlib.sha256(png).hexdigest();report['png_bytes']=len(png)\n report['completed'].append('render');report['stage']='decode'\n with Image.open(io.BytesIO(png))as image:\n  report['image_size']=list(image.size)\n  report['rgb_extrema']=ImageStat.Stat(image.convert('RGB')).extrema\n  report['stage']='geometry';assert image.size==(1280,800)\n  report['completed'].append('geometry');report['stage']='glyphs'\n  assert any(high>0 for low,high in report['rgb_extrema']),'Glyphs were not rendered'\n report['completed'].append('glyphs');report.update(ok=True,stage='complete')\nexcept BaseException as error:\n failure=error\n report['error']={'type':type(error).__name__,'message':str(error),'traceback':traceback.format_exc()}\n raise\nfinally:\n try:(out/'capture.json').write_text(json.dumps(report,indent=2)+'\\n')\n except BaseException as error:\n  if failure is None:raise\n  print('Diagnostic write failed: '+type(error).__name__+': '+str(error),file=sys.stderr)\n'''\n\n\ndef owned_counters(module: Any, sandbox: Any) -> dict[str, int]:\n    raw = module.command([\"sudo\", \"-n\", \"iptables-save\", \"-c\", \"-t\", \"filter\"])\n    result = {}\n    for line in raw.splitlines():\n        match = re.fullmatch(r\"\\[(\\d+):\\d+\\] (.*)\", line)\n        if match and (match[2].startswith(\"-A \" + sandbox.chain + \" \") or\n                      \" -i \" + sandbox.bridge + \" \" in match[2]):\n            result[match[2]] = int(match[1])\n    return result\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    trusted = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n    path = trusted / \".github/agent/capture_isolation.py\"\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"fixed_native_isolation_transport\", path)\n    if spec is None or spec.loader is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Trusted probe transport missing\")\n    isolation = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    spec.loader.exec_module(isolation)\n    module = isolation.trusted_module(\"capture_sandbox\")\n    artifact = isolation.trusted_module(\"capture_artifact\")\n    version = os.environ[\"PROBE_PYTHON\"]\n    if version not in module.IMAGES:\n        raise ValueError(\"Unsupported native probe Python line\")\n    output = Path(os.environ[\"RUNNER_TEMP\"]) / (\"atk-native-probe-\" + uuid.uuid4().hex)\n    output.mkdir(mode=0o700)\n    logs = output / \"isolation-diagnostics\"\n    logs.mkdir(mode=0o700)\n    candidate = output.parent / (\"atk-native-synthetic-\" + uuid.uuid4().hex)\n    candidate.mkdir(mode=0o700)\n    sandbox = module.Sandbox(candidate, trusted, logs / \"ownership.json\", version)\n    report: dict[str, Any] = {\"kind\": \"native-container-infrastructure-probe\",\n        \"visual_approval\": False, \"ok\": False, \"python_line\": version,\n        \"source_head\": os.environ[\"GITHUB_SHA\"], \"run_id\": os.environ[\"GITHUB_RUN_ID\"],\n        \"run_attempt\": os.environ[\"GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT\"], \"phases\": [],\n        \"source_files\": {p.name: hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n                         for p in (path, Path(__file__), path.with_name(\"capture_sandbox.py\"),\n                                   path.with_name(\"capture_artifact.py\"),\n                                   trusted / \"agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_render.py\")}}\n    identity = {\"candidate\": os.environ[\"GITHUB_SHA\"], \"repository\": os.environ[\"GITHUB_REPOSITORY\"],\n                \"run_id\": int(os.environ[\"GITHUB_RUN_ID\"]), \"run_attempt\": int(os.environ[\"GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT\"])}\n    listener = socket.socket()\n    listener.bind((\"0.0.0.0\", 0))\n    listener.listen(4)\n    listener.settimeout(0.2)\n    # Positive control proves the credential-free synthetic host endpoint is listening.\n    with socket.create_connection((\"127.0.0.1\", listener.getsockname()[1]), timeout=2):\n        accepted, _address = listener.accept()\n        accepted.close()\n\n    def interrupted(_number: int, _frame: Any) -> None:\n        raise TimeoutError(\"Native infrastructure probe interrupted\")\n\n    signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, interrupted)\n    signal.signal(signal.SIGALRM, interrupted)\n    signal.alarm(15 * 60)\n    before: dict[str, int] | None = None\n    try:\n        sandbox.setup()\n        report[\"image\"] = sandbox.image\n        network = json.loads(module.command([\"docker\", \"network\", \"inspect\", sandbox.network_id]))[0]\n        settings = {\"gateway\": network[\"IPAM\"][\"Config\"][0][\"Gateway\"],\n                    \"port\": listener.getsockname()[1], \"python\": [int(x) for x in version.split(\".\")]}\n        before = owned_counters(module, sandbox)\n        report[\"firewall_before\"] = before\n        for phase, program in ((\"probe\", INSTALL), (\"capture\", CAPTURE)):\n            python = \"python\" if phase == \"probe\" else \"/work/.venv/bin/python\"\n            container = sandbox.create(phase, [python, \"-c\", program, json.dumps(settings)], identity)\n            sandbox.verify()\n            sandbox.validate_container(container)\n            phase_logs = logs / (phase + \"-streams\")\n            phase_logs.mkdir(mode=0o700)\n            outcome = isolation.contained_output(container, phase, phase_logs, 360,\n                                                  quarantine_root=output.parent)\n            outcome[\"stream_directory\"] = phase + \"-streams\"\n            report[\"phases\"].append(outcome)\n            sandbox.remove(container)\n            if not outcome[\"ok\"]:\n                raise ValueError(\"Native contained \" + phase + \" failed\")\n        after = owned_counters(module, sandbox)\n        input_rules = [key for key in after if key.startswith(\"-A INPUT \")]\n        metadata_rules = [key for key in after if \" -d 169.254.0.0/16 \" in key]\n        if not input_rules or not metadata_rules or any(\n            after[key] <= before.get(key, 0) for key in [*input_rules, *metadata_rules]\n        ):\n            raise ValueError(\"Host/metadata refusals did not hit the owned native firewall guards\")\n        try:\n            unexpected, _address = listener.accept()\n        except TimeoutError:\n            pass\n        else:\n            unexpected.close()\n            raise ValueError(\"Contained probe reached synthetic host endpoint\")\n        report.update(ok=True, firewall_after=after)\n    except (Exception, KeyboardInterrupt) as exc:\n        report[\"error\"] = type(exc).__name__ + \": \" + str(exc)\n    finally:\n        signal.alarm(90)\n        if sandbox.rules:\n            try:\n                report[\"firewall_after\"] = owned_counters(module, sandbox)\n            except (Exception, KeyboardInterrupt) as exc:\n                report.update(ok=False, firewall_counter_error=type(exc).__name__ + \": \" + str(exc))\n        else:\n            report[\"firewall_counters_incomplete\"] = \"No established owned guards available\"\n        try:\n            sandbox.cleanup()\n            report[\"cleanup_complete\"] = True\n        except (Exception, KeyboardInterrupt) as exc:\n            report.update(ok=False, cleanup_complete=False, cleanup_error=str(exc))\n        listener.close()\n        signal.alarm(0)\n    report[\"uncertain_operations\"] = sandbox.uncertain_operations()\n    if (report.get(\"cleanup_complete\") is True and not sandbox.containers\n            and not report[\"uncertain_operations\"] and not isolation.UNSAFE_LOG_WRITER.is_set()):\n        try:\n            isolation.collect(candidate / \"probe-evidence\", output / \"probe-evidence\", artifact)\n            report[\"evidence_collected\"] = True\n        except (Exception, KeyboardInterrupt) as exc:\n            report.update(ok=False, collection_error=type(exc).__name__ + \": \" + str(exc))\n    else:\n        report.update(ok=False, collection_refused=\"Cleanup or writer absence cannot be established\")\n    (logs / \"native-probe.json\").write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    if not isolation.UNSAFE_LOG_WRITER.is_set():\n        with Path(os.environ[\"GITHUB_OUTPUT\"]).open(\"a\") as stream:\n            stream.write(\"artifact_root=\" + str(output) + \"\\n\")\n    if not report[\"ok\"]:\n        raise SystemExit(\"Native infrastructure probe failed; no activation or visual approval\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n~~~~\n\n[2] FULL 45 renderer: agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_render.py @467768b9bed2c90a0dfba85ef2eea6ac6868f8d6 | whole bytes=833 sha256=2284b4c7bc162ed0c408ed033c637a3adcd4743cab615aab6ecf44e67fe0ac07\n~~~~\n\"\"\"Choose an installed Linux monospace family for headless SVG rendering.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import TypedDict\n\n\nclass RenderOptions(TypedDict, total=False):\n    \"\"\"Supported optional renderer arguments.\"\"\"\n\n    monospace_family: str\n    font_files: list[str]\n\n\ndef render_options() -> RenderOptions:\n    \"\"\"Preserve platform defaults unless the known Debian font is available.\"\"\"\n    font = Path(\"/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSansMono.ttf\")\n    if sys.platform.startswith(\"linux\") and font.is_file():\n        # resvg-py 0.5 selects Liberation Mono for generic monospace on Linux.\n        # Bookworm's Python image contains DejaVu instead; name and load it.\n        return {\"monospace_family\": \"DejaVu Sans Mono\", \"font_files\": [str(font)]}\n    return {}\n~~~~\n\n[3] PARTIAL 44 original-font render and failure finalization: .github/agent/capture_isolation_probe.py @441a9bd825e88414c9215f7e0717e97179c77539 | whole bytes=15238 sha256=4a365793a82be8019eedb1cd83d2f6d7a5178e8d2b5bd5d17e036336bf767ae9\nExact lines 105–132 bytes=1790 sha256=3d24f5d9c49f3466422c789150ffee6e52d1f9fefda8f0c87b5bace9744b197f\n~~~~\n assert fonts,'No system fonts available for actual glyph rendering'\n report['completed'].append('fonts');report['stage']='render'\n svg='<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1280\" heigh