b0fd2cfee0783a5fac4aa17ec14fbb0d91a2dd0b5f1283576e93bca8543d733\",\n    \"bytes\": 37857\n  },\n  \"actual_result\": \"Independently read actual GitHub run39156866390, attempt1 jobs and both artifact metadata. Run completed success on467. Python3.13 job117761781940 and Python3.11 job117761782102 each succeeded. Ordinary probe-only jobs skipped by design; they do not attest ordinary GitHub CI success. This is a new actual467 run, not transferred parent4143 execution.\",\n  \"full_artifact_assessment\": [\n    \"Rehashed both supplied manifests against index entries, exact local ZIP size/hash against GitHub artifact digest, correct artifact run/head metadata and unexpired state. Verified all eight unique safe ZIP members, bounded sizes/types/names, CRC through read, exact extracted-original bytes and manifest SHA/length. No artifact or candidate content was executed.\",\n    \"Parsed complete native/capture/install/ownership records. Native source_head, run_id and run_attempt are exactly467/39156866390/1. Recorded five source hashes match the independently reviewed467 source. Actual capture program in durable create journal equals the previously independently verified published program, unchanged in467.\",\n    \"Each actual create journal carries CANDIDATE467 and run39156866390/attempt1, UID/GID1001 and explicit nonsecret environment; installation uses its owned network while capture uses none. No GitHub token, Actions runtime token or command-file environment is forwarded.\",\n    \"Both actual phases exit0, outputs complete, readers stopped, logs safe, no timeout/interruption/collection/lifecycle errors. Reassembled every retained stream and verified full SHA/count/retained_complete. Read full raw stdout/stderr: successful public Pillow12.3.0/resvg0.5.0 installation, only Git-init hints and pip notices, no hidden execution failure. Capture zero-byte streams are explicit empty SHA/parts.\",\n    \"Install reports all identity/Git/venv/pip/private-egress/IPv6 stages complete, nonroot1001, effective capabilities0, no-new-privileges1. Capture reports imports/network/fonts/render/geometry/glyph stages complete, only loopback interface and network none, actual private/IPv4/IPv6 refusals.\",\n    \"On each Python line, owned host INPUT and metadata169.254/16 REJECT counters each increase0→3. ENETUNREACH/EINVAL observations remain bounded refusal facts, not claims of native ip6tables counter hits.\",\n    \"All34 durable resource operations per line confirmed. Final containers[], network_id null, rules[], chain_created false; cleanup_complete true, uncertain_operations[], evidence_collected true. These are actual reviewed-source journal/readback outcomes; no later access to destroyed runners is claimed.\"\n  ],\n  \"glyph_and_font_measurements\": {\n    \"helper_sha256\": \"2284b4c7bc162ed0c408ed033c637a3adcd4743cab615aab6ecf44e67fe0ac07\",\n    \"font_path\": \"/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSansMono.ttf\",\n    \"font_sha256\": \"0f5db4f1749979d961019838b160bec74abdf7f9eca69553fe1aa856bbff49a4\",\n    \"actual_family_style\": [\n      \"DejaVu Sans Mono\",\n      \"Book\"\n    ],\n    \"actual_options\": {\n      \"monospace_family\": \"DejaVu Sans Mono\",\n      \"font_files\": [\n        \"/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSansMono.ttf\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"SVG_sha256\": \"c8650fff8b03cf00240ed45b8a8681f2c3a057865c71aed0e6b4c9ccf4503540\",\n    \"PNG_sha256\": \"ff19a6b3e12e84eb5fba70dcd011a8af96e1b22e32147c58b01f2b21d51f51b2\",\n    \"PNG_bytes\": 9844,\n    \"PNG_header_dimensions\": [\n      1280,\n      800\n    ],\n    \"actual_RGB_extrema\": [\n      [\n        0,\n        255\n      ],\n      [\n        0,\n        255\n      ],\n      [\n        0,\n        255\n      ]\n    ],\n    \"individual_image_review\": \"Opened BOTH full original1280x800 PNGs individually with view_image, one for3.11 and one for3.13, despite identicalhash. Both show complete readable white Probe glyphs Ag09 on black at top left, without clipping. Both receive a pass for synthetic infrastructure glyph rendering only.\",\n    \"prior_comparison_limit\": \"The complete current capture/install records and resolved image identities independently equal the corresponding genuine4143 positives. Prior independently reverified44 failure used the same image/Python/Pillow/resvg/font inventory/SVG but default family and blacke72a output; shared DejaVu policy now actually passes on467 as well. This is bounded native font/glyph acceptance, not every Unicode glyph, platform or full product scene.\"\n  },\n  \"artifact_reviews\": [\n    {\n      \"python_line\": \"3.13\",\n      \"actual_python\": \"3.13.16 (main, Oct  6 2026, 04:40:45) [GCC 12.2.0]\",\n      \"job_id\": 117761781940,\n      \"artifact_id\": 12147103860,\n      \"manifest_sha256\": \"cccae2684d87ab12d64f825ac9b5c3bc755f53a3bd82927543157099ba7a003f\",\n      \"ZIP_sha256\": \"b9cab1e58f77df2aaf9bc4a4ff7bc9669f33c2a5d2e3b20431104f1fc4248fe7\",\n      \"all8_members_verified\": true,\n      \"actual_image\": \"sha256:2a66f41838f79d3cd5c7eb749304d18d6660d0cf8547f6f38a258ffa2854ed4e\",\n      \"individual_full_original_PNG_opened\": true,\n      \"synthetic_glyph_verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"owned_host_metadata_counter_deltas\": {\n        \"-A INPUT -i atkv004ff3d892 -j REJECT --reject-with icmp-port-unreachable\": 3,\n        \"-A ATKV004ff3d892bc4fd8a8b9 -d 169.254.0.0/16 -j REJECT --reject-with icmp-port-unreachable\": 3\n      },\n      \"all34_resource_operations_confirmed_final_empty\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"python_line\": \"3.11\",\n      \"actual_python\": \"3.11.17 (main, Oct  6 2026, 04:41:03) [GCC 12.2.0]\",\n      \"job_id\": 117761782102,\n      \"artifact_id\": 12147039221,\n      \"manifest_sha256\": \"b2ea60d8ddd1c08618b2ed37e82a126ffd7f624b9f1b634651574b203d543227\",\n      \"ZIP_sha256\": \"7fb34c41873b81192711c3d82799c9cc8515471405088fd8770f2af58ae0c8bd\",\n      \"all8_members_verified\": true,\n      \"actual_image\": \"sha256:bf91cbbb4f6b3105745c0526dc4bfc7226d8bd39e5df5f59882c8bca3f787b8f\",\n      \"individual_full_original_PNG_opened\": true,\n      \"synthetic_glyph_verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"owned_host_metadata_counter_deltas\": {\n        \"-A INPUT -i atkvdaf451f670 -j REJECT --reject-with icmp-port-unreachable\": 3,\n        \"-A ATKVdaf451f6702f475bb224 -d 169.254.0.0/16 -j REJECT --reject-with icmp-port-unreachable\": 3\n      },\n      \"all34_resource_operations_confirmed_final_empty\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\n    \"Ordinary exact-final-head GitHub CI and independent full source/head/dev/task bindings remain separate; this report does not attest ordinary CI.\",\n    \"Full SQL Explorer46-scene geometry and all individual application PNG verdicts remain separate product acceptance. Synthetic glyph images grant no palette/layout/PR9 underline approval.\",\n    \"Private enrolled-machine/trusted-App provenance, genuine protected owner/delegated exact-head decision, security/authentication and owner veto/cancel/other legitimate holds remain. Native success and SSH presence/no_user do not establish enrollment trust or protected approval.\",\n    \"Trusted-main capture/probe/exporter/helper pairing requires separately reviewed exact automation-only projection and operational activation. No package UI reaches main outside release; no main/runtime action is authorized here.\",\n    \"Preserve the complete parent task, no heavy Pi candidate execution, active PR9 writer ownership, PR10/PR9 actual dev-merge/ancestry and monitoring until all qualifying PRs/successors actually merge successfully into dev.\"\n  ],\n  \"authority_limits\": {\n    \"actual467_native_infrastructure_gate_passed\": true,\n    \"reviewer_candidate_artifact_or_test_execution\": false,\n    \"reviewer_source_edits_remote_mutation_dispatch\": false,\n    \"ordinary_CI_success\": false,\n    \"full_application_visual_or_PR9_underline_approval\": false,\n    \"enrollmenttrust_protected_owner_approval_or_hold_clearance\": false,\n    \"main_runtime_activation_or_PR_merge\": false,\n    \"all_PRs_complete\": false\n  }\n}\n~~~~"],"decisions":[{"choice":"journal_error_status: Existing error message (Recommended)\nReason: The reader already returns page.warning on failure and an empty warning for successful zero-result reads. The assigned journal-error PNG confirms the misleading combined status. Showing the warning alone fixes this demonstrated issue under the request to fix issues along the way. Focused failure/recovery coverage, fresh complete GitHub visual review and exact-head validation remain required. PR #39 and the complete parent objective remain intact, including monitoring and repairs until all relevant PRs merge successfully into dev, notification limits, lifecycle labels and owner authority gates. No Pi execution or protected approval is authorized.","questions":["1. How should this repair distinguish journal read failures from successful searches with zero results, while preserving PR #39 and the complete parent objective?\nExisting error message (Recommended): Show page.warning alone on failure; retain the empty-result message for successful zero-result reads. Add focused failure/recovery coverage and require fresh complete GitHub visual review and exact-head validation.\nExplicit failure field: Add a defaulted failure indicator to JournalPage, update its reader and UI consumers, and test compatibility alongside the same visual and GitHub validation gates."]},{"choice":"completion_placement: Anchor below row (Recommended)\nReason: The pinned completion PNGs show menus overlapping the active SQL row, and source positions them using an offset without full parent-coordinate conversion. Accounting for the rendered caret row, ruler and scrolling, with above-row fallback, addresses this demonstrated issue under 'fix any issues on the way' and the reliable-fix requirement. Focused geometry/interaction regressions and fresh complete GitHub visual review remain required, alongside final-head validation and independent review. This leaf repair preserves PR #39 and the complete parent objective: all relevant PRs and resulting repairs must merge successfully into dev; retain notification limits, lifecycle labels, recorded question/answer context, concurrency and orchestrator requirements, dependency gates and owner authority. No Pi execution, protected exact-head approval, or plan/code approval is granted.","questions":["1. How should the repair position SQL completion menus while preserving PR #39 and the complete parent objective?\nAnchor below row (Recommended): Use the rendered caret row in the menu parent’s coordinates, accounting for the ruler and scrolling; keep the active row unobscured, fit above when needed, and add focused geometry and interaction regressions plus fresh full GitHub visual review."]},{"choice":"ci_repair_approach: Stable geometry and assertions (Recommended)\nReason: The request authorizes fixing issues along the way and requires a reliable repair. Stable parent-relative placement and settled sizing address the popup positioning logic while retaining containment and active-row non-overlap guarantees. Recorded CI evidence supports comparing journal display text compatibly; this must preserve exact expected text and failure/recovery behavior. Fixing lint/type findings without weakening gates preserves required validation. Fresh complete GitHub visual review, focused regressions, independent plan and implementation reviews, and final-head CI remain mandatory; assigned evidence validates neither unpublished edits nor a future head. Preserve PR #39’s existing changes and dependencies and continue the complete parent monitoring/repair objective until all relevant PRs merge successfully into dev. Retain notification limits, concurrency 10, agent:writing labels, complete question/answer records, authenticated GitHub/Telegram responses, resolver and orchestrator requirements, and the GitHub-agent-only relevance restriction for self_host. No local/Pi execution, credentials decision, owner veto/cancel decision, protected exact-head approval, or plan/code approval is granted.","questions":["1. How should PR #39’s current-head CI failures be repaired while preserving its existing changes and the complete parent objective?\nStable geometry and assertions (Recommended): Use a stable parent-relative popup origin and settled layout sizing; preserve containment/non-overlap guards, compare journal display text compatibly, and fix new lint/type findings without weakening gates. Require focused regressions, full fresh GitHub visual review, independent reviews and final-head CI; retain all parent monitoring and authority requirements."]},{"choice":"picker_text_repair: Repair text fidelity (Recommended)\nReason: The request authorizes fixing issues along the way and requires reliable prevention. Source picker.py contains the correct '.connections' heading, while the assigned full database-picker PNG for published head 6aefc2eff5e37b6d3e98a819ed00b40c9fb244d7 visibly loses its c. Tracing and repairing the responsible application/export layer with a focused regression addresses the demonstrated defect without inventing its cause. Fresh complete GitHub visual review, independent plan/source review and final-head CI remain required; existing evidence validates neither unpublished changes nor a future head. Preserve PR #39's existing changes, settled CI repair, dependencies and the root monitoring/repair objective until all relevant PRs merge successfully into dev, including notification limits, concurrency 10, agent:writing labels, complete question/answer records, authenticated GitHub/Telegram responses, resolver/orchestrator requirements and the GitHub-agent-only self_host restriction. No local/Pi execution, credentials decision, owner veto/cancellation decision, protected exact-head approval or plan/code approval is granted.","questions":["1. How should PR #39 