full visual/source validation and monitoring through all qualifying dev merges."]},{"choice":"pr39_ci_diagnostic_strategy: Bounded GitHub diagnostics (Recommended)\nReason: The recorded request authorizes reliable repairs along the way, and its authenticated diagnostics-first correction supports coordinator-owned isolated GitHub evidence before cause-specific planning. Candidate/dev/task/run-bound geometry and removal-lifecycle diagnostics across both supported Textual lines address the stated uncertainty without guessing causes or requiring owner-supplied evidence. Readiness, viewport-edge and lint repairs remain contingent on verified evidence and fresh independent plan review; this assessment does not establish those causes. Preserve incoming dev coordinator code/tests/docs, existing and unpublished PR39 repairs, warning-only journal failure/recovery behavior, exact picker heading, completion containment/non-overlap, regressions, quality/coverage baselines, all 46 full-scene geometry and individual PNG gates, independent full-feature/source review and exact-final-head CI. Retain PR39/PR37, exporter/producer-consumer/activation and PR10/PR9 merge/ancestry dependencies. Continue monitoring and repairs until every qualifying PR merges successfully into dev. Retain concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels including agent:writing, complete questions/options/answers, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies, independent resolver assessment, the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit, GitHub-agent-only self_host relevance and notification limits. No local/Pi execution is authorized. Genuine owner input, credentials, provenance/security, veto/cancel and protected exact-head holds remain intact. This approves only the recommended strategy's alignment, not a plan, code, protected action, deployment or completion claim.","questions":["1. How should planning resolve PR #39’s remaining resize/lifecycle CI uncertainty while preserving its settled repairs and complete parent objective?\nBounded GitHub diagnostics (Recommended): Have the coordinator obtain candidate/dev/task/run-bound geometry and removal-lifecycle diagnostics through isolated GitHub validation for both supported Textual lines. Preserve incoming dev coordinator code/tests/docs, existing PR changes, warning-only journal status, viewport containment/non-overlap, all 46 visual gates and all parent monitoring/authority requirements. Use the evidence to finish cause-specific planning and independent plan review; repair verified readiness, viewport-edge and lint test issues without weakening assertions. No Pi execution or owner-provided evidence."]},{"choice":"pr39_diagnostic_execution_path: Candidate-push diagnostics (Recommended)\nReason: The full retained owner request requires reliable repairs, no heavy checks onPi, and monitoring until every qualifying PR and resulting repair merges successfully into dev. The existing independently resolved diagnostics-first strategy requires candidate/base/task-bound GitHub evidence across both supported Textual lines before selecting causes. The current operational handoff identifies a real execution-path gap: the ordinary test workflow currently persists checkout credentials and has no diagnostic dispatch inputs, while the protected visual workflow only captures Python3.11 scenes. Selecting a bounded ordinary-tests-workflow opt-in diagnostic path on existing agent-visual/<sha> pushes, with checkout credential persistence disabled, concretizes that already selected strategy without inventing dispatch inputs or changing protected controller/dispatch/visual workflows. Python3.11/Textual0.73 andPython3.13/Textual0.89 diagnostic jobs supplement, rather than replace or relax, normal required CI. Ordered instrumentation, full Ruff output and always-retained failures/log/provenance artifacts address the evidence gap even when assertions fail, while preserving strict assertions, complete original failure results and meaningful regression/coverage gates. Independent review of the complete renewed plan is required before instrumentation; resulting exact-bound GitHub evidence then informs separate cause-specific planning and review. This is an implementation-sequence choice within existing repair authorization, not a request for a new owner fact, credentials, protected approval or hold release.\n\nTransparent automated coordinator response after separate independent full-task assessment under the owner's standing recommended-options policy. This selects the diagnostic execution strategy only. The renewed complete plan must explicitly limit candidate execution to isolated GitHub runners with read-only permissions and no persisted/write credentials, secrets or privileged controller context available to candidate code; persist-credentials:false is required and is not by itself a complete credential-isolation claim. Limit workflow changes to the ordinary tests workflow; preserve protected controller, dispatch, capture/visual and publishing workflows and genuine exact-head authority boundaries. Use only the actual existing temporary-candidate publication mechanism with exact SHA checks and narrowly activated diagnostics; do not invent unsupported dispatch inputs or infer new publishing rights.\n\nKeep ordinary CI triggers, required matrix, assertions, exit status/aggregate failure reporting, coverage/debt floors and strictness intact. The extra diagnostic matrix must retain ordered records, each scenario's original inputs/failure/traceback, framework source+installed version provenance, complete stdout/stderr and Ruff findings even when assertions stop a scenario, and an always-retained bounded artifact index. If a controlled diagnostic runner continues other cases to collect evidence, it must still record and propagate all original failures; no continue-on-error success, hidden truncation, missing-entry-as-pass, forced scene state, relaxed assertion or substituted expected number. Bind source PR/head, 